CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*std::optional<tag-S>::optional\(this,rref_struct_tag\(identifier=tag-S\)\).*$
^.*std::optional<tag-S>::optional\(this,ref_struct_tag\(identifier=tag-S\)\).*$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct optional'.*$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct S &'.*$
--
Regression for per-call deduction and ranking of a forwarding-reference
converting constructor (std::optional<S>'s optional(_Up&&)).  An lvalue
construction (optional(S&)) followed by a prvalue construction must
re-deduce optional(S&&) for the prvalue, not reuse the cached
optional(S&).  Covers [over.match.viable] (non-viable candidate is
excluded, not a hard error) and [over.best.ics]/[over.match.best]
(ICS quality is ranked before the non-template tie-breaker; a copy
constructor reachable only via a second user-defined conversion must
not win).  Verified at the goto-program level.
